                <pb facs="0357" n="1425" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v05p2/pg1425"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>During the morning of Saturday, October 23, Dulles, accompanied by General
                    Gruenther, spoke with Eden and Macmillan concerning the stationing of their
                    troops in Trieste, and the British gave the impression that these troops would
                    not be sent to Austria but would be brought home. Dulles then spoke with Eden
                    about the British pledge to help finance UNRRA. Summaries of the discussion of
                    these two subjects were transmitted to the Department of State in telegrams
                    Dulte 14 and 15 from Paris, October 23; telegram Dulte 14 is printed in the
                    compilation on Austria in <ref target="frus:frus1952-54v07p1">volume VII</ref>.
                    Telegram Dulte 15, not printed, is in Department of State file
                    357.AD/10–2354.</p>
            </div>
